      "content": "\"Goblin's intuition\" is not a legal term. Please provide the actual technical criteria or the specific case law precedents HMRC uses to evaluate whether a nominee arrangement is a legitimate agency relationship or an artificial structure. Specifically, what indicators—such as control over bank accounts, voting rights, or the ability to remove trustees—are used to determine if the nominee is a mere conduit for the settlor?",
